@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# OKX US historical candles
+
+Backtest Lab sends `market_data_source: "okx_us"` for new runs. This selects the
+fixed US public endpoint `https://us.okx.com/api/v5/market/history-candles`.
+Existing configs without a source retain Binance, so reloading an old run does
+not silently change its market data. Run configs persist the selected source;
+the backtest chart uses that same source.
+
+`BTCUSDT`, `ETHUSDT`, and `SOLUSDT` map to USDT perpetual instruments such as
+`BTC-USDT-SWAP`. Requests need no exchange account or API key. This reader does
+not construct a trader or change the endpoint used by live exchange accounts.
+It does not follow redirects or fall back to another region/provider.
+
+The reader paginates backward using exclusive `after` cursors, then deduplicates
+and sorts. It includes only confirmed candles closed by the acquisition cutoff.
+NOFX separately limits every AI snapshot to candles closed at simulation time;
+the next candle remains available only for simulated execution. Perpetual volume
+uses `volCcy` (base currency), not `vol` (contracts). Longer bars use UTC variants.
+
+The shared request gate limits this process to five requests per second. HTTP or
+API failures are surfaced, including access denial and rate limiting.
+
+Contract: [official OKX US API documentation](https://app.okx.com/docs-v5/en/#order-book-trading-market-data-get-candlesticks-history),
+[regional API domains](https://www.okx.com/docs-v5).
+
+Run deterministic fixture tests with:
+
+```sh
+go test -race ./market/okxhistory ./market ./backtest \
+  -run 'TestRange|TestMappings|TestFailures|TestMalformed|TestPagination|TestConflicting|TestHistorical' \
+  -count=1
+```
+
+Public network smoke checks are separate from these tests. Check 3m, 15m, and 4h
+candles through the declared regional endpoint after deployment. If denied, stop
+and diagnose access; do not use another region or provider automatically.
